## 19. Windows Permissions – ACLs

Windows uses **Access Control Lists (ACLs)**.

ACLs specify what access different users and groups have to an object.

Examples include:
- Read.
- Write.
- Modify.
- Read & Execute.
- Full Control.

Windows ACLs allow more detailed permissions than the simpler Unix permission model.

### Useful Commands

View permissions:

```powershell
Get-Acl .\file.txt
```

View permissions using `icacls`:

```powershell
icacls file.txt
```

Take ownership:

```powershell
takeown /f file.txt
```

Ownership and ACL modifications can affect security and should be performed only when needed.

